          <Pad Id="XoV7SCmdHTAzTHIDtRUbI2" Bounds="73,87,471,33" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Hull From Point Groups / Physical 3d Text">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">16</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="nu4bqT0qGZ8wgdrabAODN7" Bounds="73,136,903,211" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Async pipeline of VL.Stride.Text3d and VL.Stride.BepuPhysics: The glyphs of one sentence rain down onto the typed text.&#xD;&#xA;Text3dMeshes (Async) extrudes one mesh per glyph on a background thread; with Compute Points enabled it also outputs the distinct vertex positions per glyph (text local space).&#xD;&#xA;Standing text: HullsFromPointGroups (Async) bakes one hull per glyph into a single collider on the text entity's Static.&#xD;&#xA;Falling text: Per glyph, HullFromPoints (Async) bakes the glyph's group and the ConvexHullCollider's Position Local is set to the negated glyph translation, which shifts the text local hull into glyph local space so it matches the glyph mesh on its Body. The glyph translation comes from applying the glyph transformation to the zero vector; it also places the spawn position, so the sentence falls in formation.&#xD;&#xA;Hulls are convex per glyph, so counters (the holes in e, o, a, ...) are filled in by design. &#xD;&#xA;In Progress pins report background activity; while a bake runs the last completed result stays active. &#xD;&#xA;The only remaining main thread work is the engine's hull build when a collider attaches.&#xD;&#xA;ColliderShapes draws the baked per glyph hulls.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
